# Copy this file to frontend.env on the VPS (next to docker-compose.prod.yml).
# It can stay empty for now — the frontend currently reads exactly one env
# var (NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL), and that one is inlined into the JS bundle at
# `docker build` time (see .github/workflows/deploy.yml's build-args), not
# read from this file at container runtime. This file exists so
# docker-compose.prod.yml's env_file has something to point at, and so
# there's already a place to add a real server-only runtime secret later
# without touching the compose file again.
